This actually works as described, though it was so
high risk it took me a couple of thousand turns to
get from HP 13 to HP 15 to HP 18, in two prayers,
with one food prayer required in between. I ended
up at HP:30 after quaffing my potions, none of them
blessed, and a couple of stray healings since have
upped that to HP:32.

I went on to conquer Mines Town _first_, in this
game, and just finished Sokoban and exited. This
is one of those games that _any_ competent NetHack
player should be able to win.

Highlights:

Now at XL:1/15.

AC: -19, naked AC: -1; I was able to donate about
16,000 zorkmids total, in the Mines Town with the
two trees and four shops, what with having cleaned
out a fairly deep vault for over 1000z after having
acquired a broad pick and lied through my teeth to
the vault guard, and thereby arrived at Mines Town
with over 5000z (I also bankrupted a shopkeeper
along the way). This gave me two AC improvements
past the standard 9. Mines town was _really_
difficult, the Mines entrance was at DLVL 4, Mines
Town at DLVL 8, so the monster mix was
"interesting", including hobgoblins and floating
eyes. With only 3 mana points, I couldn't heal my
pets, spent lots of time pushing them away from the
watch captain and guards.

So far, wands of digging (2) lightning, fire, sleep,
slow monster, speed monster.

Three pets cleaned out David's Treasure zoo for me,
I just gated them in and shut the door; the two
smaller pets were able to take on the weaker monsters
and level up a bit, more advantage to keeping the
monster difficulty minimal.

This was the deepest possible Sokoban, with the
entrance at DLVL 10, so the treasure zoo was at DLVL
6, and made me very glad I'd arrived and set the
monster difficulty in part with my XL:1.

I have many, many rings, Levitation the only one
that self-IDed.

I have a magic whistle. My next goal is to return to
mines, to the level below Mines Town, and search for
a polymorph trap for upgrading my pets.

I got the amulet of reflection top level for Sokoban,
so my constantly going in and out of "burdened"
state is still an issue.

I managed to create a stash in bottom level Sokoban,
what with engrave IDing what turned out to be a wand
of fire there (sweet). There's 8 food rations and
some other goodies there.

Now I could hand this game off to _any_ regular
ascender with that kit, and they'd be good to go.

Me? YASD ahead, only the type has yet to be seen.

Oh, by the way, the DLVL under the Sokoban entrance
turned out to be a bones level Big Room. I'm really,
really not going there until I better my current AC
kit. That's the first time I've seen the Big Room in
several whole calendar years of playing.

